  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA, single profile, PCA n2000) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while config_010 (Image, single profile, ResNet50) achieves only 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant signal and leaving large uncertainty about whether multiprofile aggregation can improve the RNA baseline. Question: config_002 directly extends config_001 by switching from single to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation while keeping the same PCA n2000 encoder, cleanly isolating the effect of profile multiplicity and aggregation on RNA performance. Why this is the best next experiment: With only two data points, the highest-value question is whether the multiprofile design axis adds value over the current best single-profile setup. A positive result would justify investing further in multiprofile + aggregation variants (and ultimately multimodal multiprofile configs); a negative or neutral result would redirect effort toward encoder improvements (scvi, scgpt) or multimodal fusion with single profiles. This experiment changes only the profile/aggregation dimension relative to the current best, making it the cleanest and most informative next step under a limited budget."
}

